ther) and then multiply by 100 to change it into percent.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5311;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13147";s:6:"answer";s:350:"The caudate lobe is a (physiologically) independent part of the liver, supplied by the right and left hepatic artery and portal vein. Blood from the caudate lobe drains directly into the vena cava.It is also known as the lobule of Spiegel. The caudate section of the liver is connected to the right lobe by a narrow bridge called the caudate process.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5312;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13148";s:6:"answer";s:9:"Dendrites";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5313;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13149";s:6:"answer";s:60:"It is located at the top of Blarney Castle in Cork, Ireland.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5314;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13150";s:6:"answer";s:15:"50 working days";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5315;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13151";s:6:"answer";s:118:"Gallstone pancreatitis is inflammation of the pancreas that results from blockage of the pancreas duct by a gallstone.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5316;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13152";s:6:"answer";s:202:"The carbon dioxide in the blood is exchanged for oxygen in the alveoli. These tiny air sacs in the lungs are only one cell thick and they are surrounded by capillaries that are also only one cell thick.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5317;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13154";s:6:"answer";s:26:"Neurotoxins and Hemotoxins";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5318;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13155";s:6:"answer";s:20:"1 year and 6 months.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5319;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11:"query_13156";s:6:"answer";s:114:"They form the phospholipid membranes that surround the cell and intracellular organelles such as the mitochondria.";s:8:"category";s:2:"qa";s:5:"label";N;}i:5320;a:4:{s:8:"question";s:11